     \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_elasticache_serverless_cache It should update the state with attribute user_group_id set to null as deduced from the [resource documentation]( AWS API errors out. console \\u2502 Error: updating ElastiCache Serverless Cache (cache1-serverless) \\u2502 \\u2502 with module.elasticache_serverless[\\\"cache1\\\"].aws_elasticache_serverless_cache.elasticache, \\u2502 on .terraform/modules/elasticache_serverless/aws-elasticach\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-05-26T10:03:01Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.299,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 45204,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#45204\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_elasticache_serverless_cache recreates if engine is changed from valkey 7 to redis 7\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"aws_elasticache_serverless_cache Terraform should allow in-place valkey 7 to redis 7 engine update as AWS console allows same behaviour. It should not destroy and recreate resource. Terraform is recreating elasticache serverless. console Terraform used the selected providers to generate the following execution plan. Resource actions are indicated with the following symbols: -/+ destroy and then cr\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-11-21T16:52:27Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.296,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11817,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b8c17e-529e-4422-bbce-9be07ebac855","uuid":"ed40b593-e2c7-4e2a-8ec4-eb623eeca639","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:15:51.332Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 7,\n    \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: Support public endpoints (connection_type) for aws_elasticache_serverless_cache\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open